sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor You as You (UI or /docs)
  participant R as main.py / web.py
  participant O as orders.py
  participant I as inventory.py
  participant P as promos.py
  participant $ as pricing.py
  participant DB as SQLite

  Note over You,DB: Quote: API POST /orders/quote; form POST /performances/{id}/quote. Writes nothing.
  You->>R: cart + optional promo code
  R->>O: quote(req, now)
  O->>I: tiers_for_performance()
  I->>DB: seats sold = order lines on orders that aren't cancelled
  I-->>O: price and seats left per tier
  O->>I: check_seats() (409 if not enough)
  O->>P: find_valid_promo(code, now) (400 if unknown or expired)
  O->>$: price_order(lines, promo)
  $-->>O: subtotal, discount, fees, tax, total
  O-->>You: Quote with pricing_lines

  Note over You,DB: Order: API POST /orders; form POST /performances/{id}/orders. Prices through quote(), then writes.
  You->>R: cart + promo + email
  R->>O: create_order(req, now)
  O->>DB: lock (BEGIN IMMEDIATE)
  O->>O: quote(req, now), the same steps as above
  O->>DB: INSERT order (status paid, stored totals)
  O->>DB: INSERT order lines (price paid, captured now)
  O->>P: record_use(code): uses + 1
  O->>DB: COMMIT
  O-->>You: Order

  Note over You,DB: Cancel: API only, POST /orders/{id}/cancel. No browser cancellation form.
  You->>R: order id
  R->>O: cancel_order(id) (409 if already cancelled)
  O->>DB: UPDATE status = cancelled
  Note over I,DB: Seats free up by themselves: seat counts skip cancelled orders
